# Pins to the `except` KEYWORD on line 11, NOT to the statements on line 12.
# Changed 2026-08-16 with the @warn capture move to (kExcept): the reported line
# is where a reviewer must write an accountable `dl:ok bare-except` marker, and
# on line 12 that was the handler's first statement rather than the construct
# the rule is about. See docs/INBOX-bare-except-anchor-defeats-a-hand-written-marker.md
# and tests/autotest/run_bare_except_anchor.ps1.
bare-except 11
!empty-except
